{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A4UserV17organizationLevelSbvp","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","title":"organizationLevel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"organizationLevel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this is an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"organization-level"}]},{"type":"text","text":" principal (CONTRACT.md §5.2)."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamUser\/organizationLevel"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamuser\/organizationlevel"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"organizationLevel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Such a principal’s record lives in its organization’s reserved tenant, so its global"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grants apply in every tenant of that organization, and it can act on a different one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by sending a different "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X-Axiam-Tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" on the next request — no re-login, because it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already is a principal of every tenant there."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ordinary tenant principal is a principal of exactly one tenant; the same header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change produces a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"403"},{"text":" for it. This flag is therefore what an application checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" offering a tenant switch, rather than discovering the answer from a failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Derived, never asserted"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (§5.2 rule 2): resolved server-side from the caller’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant record, and never sent by this SDK. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" when the login response omits it —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is what a server older than contract 1.31 answers — and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" on the guard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"path, where this value is built from token claims that do not carry it. Both are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safe direction: the application then offers no cross-tenant action."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Since contract 1.35 that reach can be narrowed per assignment, so this flag alone no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"longer decides what to offer: consult ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamUser\/reachableTenantIDs","type":"reference"},{"text":" as well (§5.2.3 rule 3).","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamUser"]]},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamUser":{"u